  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Grossman joined Southern Container, a packaging company founded by his father and uncle, and spent more than four decades in the business. The group grew into a major independent producer of corrugated boxes, graphics packaging and containerboard, integrating mills and converting operations under family ownership.\n\nHe represented shareholders when RockTenn acquired the company, marking the transition from active family enterprise to investment and philanthropy. Grossman and his family endowed a business school at the University of Vermont and later made a major gift to Woods Hole Oceanographic Institution for research. Long-distance voyages sharpened his interest in marine science and environmental protection, giving his later giving a clear connection to personal experience.",
